# Crawler headless socket separates deterministic acts from presentation

`CrawlerBossSystem.step(at)` now owns the Crawler's act ladder, component inference, burst, track pin, overcharge, and relay-drain selection. `syncPresentation(at)` owns GLB loading and disposal, placeholder transforms, beam/dial/wreck scene state, and the canvas test hook. `update(at)` preserves browser order by calling those two seams in sequence.

`HeadlessContractSim` constructs the same production system for `dynamo_crawler`, steps only the simulation seam, routes wave/component events into it, and exposes diagnostics under `crawler`. The headless `crawler3dState` stays at its initial value; presentation state is deliberately excluded from the deterministic outcome hash so FULL and LITE hosts cannot diverge.

Canyon Works is now admitted at 3/4 E3 agent readiness. The repeated boss acceptance pin is `fnv1a32:f466d065`: wave 14, all three components destroyed, 18 W drain observed, secure, zero calls. The shared `(secureWave + 2)` budget and known `objectiveAllowsSecure` behavior were not changed.

Related: [[Rival Dynamo Crawler preserves three-component boss damage — 2026-07-15 0630]], [[Crawler GLB uses atlas emission for full-night damage readability — 2026-07-15 2132]], [[Canyon Works composes the E3 spine through authored pylon sites — 2026-07-15 0050]].
