# Final boss fidelity programme

Owner authorization, 2026-09-08: "Go one by one - each epoch (1 to 10) has a final boss ... focus first on the bosses ... start with the Baron of epoch one and work through them."

Active goal: improve all ten final boss presentations in epoch order, preserving their gameplay and story contracts. Work stays on `sol/boss-art-fidelity-review`; no commits, queue changes, STATUS edits or deployments are authorized by this programme. The prior [comparison review](../../reviews/sol-findings-boss-art-fidelity.md) and [gallery](../../artifacts/boss-art-fidelity-2026-09-08/index.html) establish the starting evidence.

| Epoch | Final boss | State | Required focus |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Baron | **Verified E1 pass** | Approved illustrated body stays. Improve 3D prop materials and crafted finish, launcher attachment, telegraph and rocket origin; prove in-game appearance. |
| 2 | Armored Railcar | **Verified E2 pass** | Armored cab, running gear and underbody detail; retain rail fit and component damage. |
| 3 | Dynamo Crawler | **In progress** | Tall coils, articulated insulators, drive machinery; retain three damage components. |
| 4 | Land Yacht | Pending E3 | Wheeled ship proportions, open grapple, then actual GLB adoption; currently image crops in runtime. |
| 5 | Dredge Queen | Pending E4 | Wheelhouse, armored hold, hull width, cloth sail and selective material treatment. |
| 6 | Homemaker-9000 | Pending E5 | Rounded body, flared apron, deep lens, curved vacuum; retain final chair state. |
| 7 | Echo | Pending E6 | Mirrored settlement forms and signal identity; this is an encounter presentation, not a mechanical monster. |
| 8 | Salvage King's Claw | Pending E7 | Suspended crescent claws, hanging machinery and crown hierarchy; retain airborne and civic landing states. |
| 9 | Old Digger | Pending E8 | Deep bucket wheels, industrial center and substantial trusses; retain intact gentle reprogramming. |
| 10 | Quiet | Pending E9 | Environmental absence and loss-of-meaning presentation consistent with its art; preserve encounter/site mechanics. |

Only the current epoch is implemented at a time. Subagents may examine or verify separate parts of that boss. A completed epoch requires an actual visible improvement against its reference, source/asset validation, unchanged gameplay invariants, desktop and 390px mobile evidence, relevant existing tests, and a durable review naming limitations. A loader flag or a showroom render alone is insufficient.

Each epoch's evidence lives under `artifacts/boss-fidelity/e<N>-<boss>/`, with a report in `reviews/sol-boss-fidelity-e<N>-<boss>.md`. Update this table only after inspecting that evidence. Do not call the ten-epoch goal complete until all rows have verified outcomes.

## Current handoff: E3 Dynamo Crawler

E1 and E2 completed verified fidelity passes. See [Baron review](../../reviews/sol-boss-fidelity-e1-baron.md) and [Railcar review](../../reviews/sol-boss-fidelity-e2-railcar.md). The ten-epoch goal remains active; E4–E10 are pending in order.

E3's revised candidate is exported and served: 11,760 triangles, three original component meshes and damage morphs, one embedded atlas. The geometry exposes drive wheels, adds segmented electrical fittings, unequal stacks, copper windings, curved conduits, lower capacitor chambers and a framed dynamo window. The native atlas and source receipts live under `artifacts/boss-fidelity/e3-crawler/`. Three fresh source builds and the saved-Blend re-export match SHA-256 `26112eaa095aa891d57c209e224e81a3a9fc89bc6f56614eb98ee6d5d5016eb6`.

Runtime acceptance is pending. The selected candidate uses uniform scale 3.1, fixed formation alignment, white mapped fill, a shallow terrain fit, an authored collector attachment and a silhouette-based health-bar position. The first build revealed that production quantization rebases mesh-local coordinates while preserving anchor extras: all cached support/silhouette geometry and authored anchors must use asset-root coordinates. Verify both raw and optimized GLBs before accepting E3. Component loss, suspend invariants, desktop/mobile rendering and independent runtime review remain in the final checks. The original plate depicts rail wheels while gameplay uses tracks; the revised asset retains treads and exposes their wheel rhythm. Moving-route checks then found two additional E3 issues: per-component night-speed samples accumulate formation drift, and a steep terrain tilt displaces the tall mast from its target. A common pre-step body light sample (with browser/headless parity) and fixed-height tilt pivot are under evaluation; the act-2 dial also needs a proven transparency correction. The passed spawn-view checks and 18 existing E3 tests precede those pending corrections. E4's read-only preflight is complete; implementation waits for E3 verification.

Vite on 5246 is available for evidence; no gate ports, commits, STATUS edits or existing e2e edits are needed. Only the current epoch is implemented.
